    "label": "27",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following.\n$$\\frac{x^2+6x+9}{x+3}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x+3$, $x\\ne-3$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x^2+6x+9}{x+3}&=\\frac{(x+3)^2}{x+3}\\\\\\frac{x^2+6x+9}{x+3}&=x+3.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominator requires $x\\ne-3$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
